# This repository's working tree is the whole home directory (C:\Users\ayoub),
# and its remote is public: https://github.com/ayoub1920/donation.git
#
# So this file is an ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. Everything is ignored by
# default and only the project folders this repo actually tracks are let back
# in. A denylist cannot work here: every new tool drops a new dot-directory
# into the home folder (.aws, .kube, .docker, .gnupg, .claude.json, .cagent,
# .codeium, .antigravity ...), and one `git add .` before you notice would
# publish credentials that cannot be un-published.
#
# Note: this does not untrack anything. Git ignores only untracked files, so
# every file already committed is unaffected.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TO ADD A NEW PROJECT: add a `!` line for it below, next to its siblings.
# Until you do, `git add <path>` will refuse it and tell you to use -f.
# Prefer giving the project its own repository instead — as was done for
# Desktop/Frontend_Rakeb (github.com/ayoub1920/Rakeb).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Ignore every entry at the root of the home directory.
/*

# ...except this file, so it stays visible and committable.
!/.gitignore

# 2. Re-include only the two folders that hold tracked projects.
!/Desktop/
!/Documents/

# 3. Inside them, ignore everything except the tracked projects themselves.
/Desktop/*
!/Desktop/Backend-server/
!/Desktop/premierapp/
!/Desktop/sqldeveloper/
!/Desktop/web projet/

/Documents/*
!/Documents/integration_ayoub_taha_khadija/
!/Documents/integrationn/
!/Documents/interface/
!/Documents/interface1/
!/Documents/lesinterfaces/
!/Documents/menu/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defence in depth: these apply inside the allowed project folders too, where
# secrets and build output are just as likely to appear.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Credentials and keys
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*credentials*.json
serviceAccount*.json

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
target/
dist/
build/
out/
.gradle/
.angular/
.expo/
__pycache__/
*.class

# Local tooling and editor state
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
